      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آوِ</span></b>  or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آوٍ</span>: see 2. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آوٍ</span> [the part. n. of 1] has for
its pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُوِىٌّ</span> [like one of the inf. ns. of 1]. (T, S.)
The latter is applied to birds, signifying <i>Collecting,</i> or <i>flocking, together;</i> (T, S, M, * K; *) syn.
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَأَوِّيَةٌ</span></b>  (Lth, T) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَأَوِّيَاتٌ</span>. (Lth, T, S, M, K.)

